15	 * {@code sharesHousehold: true} and an existing owner already shares the household — the same
16	 * lastName (compared case-insensitively with collapsed whitespace) and the same address, compared
17	 * in normalized form (see {@link OwnerAddress#normalize(String)}), matching
18	 * {@link CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique}, which allows the duplicate through in that case.
19	 *
20	 * <p>The identifier is a <em>stable</em> value derived deterministically from the normalized
21	 * lastName and address, so every owner in the same household receives the same id regardless of
22	 * creation order. Both the joining owner and every existing household member are updated to carry
23	 * it, so the household is linked from either side.
